From d136a6ee9645d0b507266716614593ab85091174 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HuskerMinion <28571744+HuskerMinion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/40] r8169: Add the Realtek RTD129x SoC GMAC

The RTD1293/RTD1295/RTD1296 SoCs integrate an RTL8168g family MAC with
an embedded GPHY on the RBUS. The vendor kernels drive it with
"r8169soc", a 9-10k line fork of an old r8169. The differences that
matter compared with a PCIe RTL8168g are small, so handle it in r8169
through a platform driver instead.

Decouple the core from struct pci_dev first:

- derive the struct device from the net_device parent instead of
  tp->pci_dev, and use it for DMA, runtime PM and the MDIO bus
- skip the PCI-only operations (bus mastering, CSI/ECAM config space
  access, CLKREQ, MSI detection, bus reset and ASPM recovery on Tx
  timeout, PCI error decoding) when there is no PCI device
- split the bus independent tail of the probe into rtl_init_netdev()
  and the remove/shutdown paths into rtl_remove_common() and
  rtl_shutdown_common()
- register the LED class devices only for PCI devices, since their
  names are derived from the PCI location

There is no functional change for PCI devices.

The SoC front end, behind CONFIG_R8169_RTD129X, then handles what is
different:

- The TxConfig XID (0x109) matches no PCI chip. Use RTL_GIGA_MAC_VER_42
  from the match data, as the vendor DT ("mac-version = <42>") does,
  and no PHY firmware.
- The PHY is reached through PHYAR, not GPHY_OCP (the vendor driver
  switches the 8168g OCP accessors off). Accept genphy if no dedicated
  PHY driver matches, and do not register the c45 accessors.
- PHY setup follows the vendor drivers instead of the RTL8168gu PCIe
  parameters: mask the PHY interrupts to the MAC MCU (OCP 0xfc1e)
  while configuring, set dis_mcu_clroob, enable ALDPS, and unmask them
  again after the PHY reset.
- Rx/Tx DMA bursts of 128/256 bytes as in the vendor drivers, no EPHY
  or PCIe config space accesses, 32-bit DMA.
- EEE stays off; the vendor kernels need a MAC MCU patch for it.
- The boot loader leaves the MAC address in MAC0; retry while it reads
  0xdeadbeef, as the vendor driver does. A local-mac-address in DT
  takes precedence.
- The boot loader normally leaves the GMAC clocked and out of reset.
  Otherwise run the vendor power-up sequence through the ISO syscon and
  the reset controller.
- With ALDPS enabled the GMAC powers down its Rx/Tx paths while there
  is no link ("MAC powercut"). The QNAP, Synology and Realtek BSP
  vendor drivers all schedule a MAC reset on every link-up interrupt to
  recover from that; do the same from the phylib link change handler.

None of the GMAC or ISO registers used here lie in the 0x800-0x9ff
range of the RTD129x eMMC/RBUS erratum, and the vendor drivers take no
lock.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/Kconfig      |  11 +
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c | 658 +++++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 529 insertions(+), 140 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/Kconfig b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/Kconfig
index 272c83bfd..23c954c12 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/Kconfig
@@ -113,6 +113,17 @@ config R8169
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
 	  will be called r8169.  This is recommended.
 
+config R8169_RTD129X
+	bool "Realtek RTD129x SoC integrated Gigabit Ethernet support"
+	depends on R8169 && OF
+	depends on ARCH_REALTEK || COMPILE_TEST
+	select MFD_SYSCON
+	help
+	  Say Y here to let the r8169 driver also handle the Gigabit
+	  Ethernet MAC with embedded PHY that is integrated into the
+	  Realtek RTD1293, RTD1295 and RTD1296 SoCs. It is an RTL8168g
+	  family MAC attached to the SoC bus instead of PCIe.
+
 config R8169_LEDS
 	bool "Support for controlling the NIC LEDs"
 	depends on R8169 && LEDS_TRIGGER_NETDEV
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
index 43a786ccf..4f6f892e9 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
